  "findings": [
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/plan-review/the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/r-20261118T191635934468-plan-review-of-the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/plan.html:884",
      "id": "reasoning-1",
      "reason": "the section's benefit and its place among the 10 s levers rest on a pre-s92 number, and re-measuring the pass on post-s92 code changes what the section promises and what its test must bound.",
      "text": "the section's only quantitative justification, \"9.8% of samples on every sweep\" (reproduced exactly: 223 of the profile's 2,269 samples carry a `compose_owed_plan_reviews` frame), is measured on the 06:25Z profile before s92 landed (commit `0ed05f0071`, 2026-11-18T08:05:38+01:00), and the section itself says s92 cut the reads of an unchanged pass, so the quoted share includes reads the repair no longer pays and no post-s92 residual measurement is cited",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/plan-review/the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/r-20261118T191635934468-plan-review-of-the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/plan.html:884",
      "id": "done_when-1",
      "reason": "an assertion no correct implementation can satisfy leaves the node unable to close; the done-when must instead compare per-plan decisions with elapsed time factored out, or the set of reviews composed over the interval.",
      "text": "the done-when asserts \"Every pass composes the same reviews with the same skip reasons as the base revision\", but the pass writes elapsed age into its reasons (`int(age // 60)` minutes, plan_review.py:4877; quiet-period reason at 4703) and weighs one plan per pass under a persisted cursor (`PLAN_REVIEW_PASS_LIMIT = 1`, plan_review.py:4110), so a pass delayed by up to the stated 60 s is later than base's pass and base's repeated passes advance a rotation the gated run does not, making the recorded reasons differ by construction",
      "type": "done_when",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/plan-review/the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/r-20261118T191635934468-plan-review-of-the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/plan.html:884",
      "id": "done_when-2",
      "reason": "the untested trigger is part of the deliverable and the pass already reads authoring runs (`plan_authoring_runs`, plan_review.py:4845), so an arm that changes one is what proves the third signal fires.",
      "text": "the deliverable names three change triggers (\"a plan file, a stored plan review or a plan-authoring run\"), but the done-when exercises the plan file and the pass itself reads authoring runs (`plan_authoring_runs`, plan_review.py:4845); an implementation that never watches that input passes every arm",
      "type": "done_when",
      "would_change": true
    }
  ],
