  "rubric_items": {
    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 `plan_review.compose_owed_plan_reviews` (plan_review.py:4745), `resumption.sweep` (resumption.py:2704) and its call site (resumption.py:3058) resolve at head c09105f5; the cited profile resolves and its 2,269 samples match the section.",
    "done_when": "findings \u2014 s100's negative control is sound, but its base-equality assertion cannot hold and one of its three declared triggers is never exercised.",
    "evidence_paths": "pass \u2014 the cited profile exists at `~/.cache/reckon-landing/station-prof-0625-post-s90.raw` (598,821 bytes) and each arm's log sits under the run directory, not a node-local temporary path.",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 the named module paths and test file carry no plan label, section id or ticket number.",
    "reasoning": "a finding \u2014 s100's 9.8% justification is read from a profile taken at 06:25Z, before s92, the change that cut the pass's reads, landed at 07:05Z, so the cited cost is not the cost this section removes.",
    "single_goal": "pass \u2014 s100 carries one deliverable, gating the owed-plan-review pass on a 60 s maximum interval, with both change signals and the fallback serving that deliverable.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 s100 has no depends-on entry in `plan-section-depends-on` (snapshot plan.html:23), which matches its inputs: s92, whose read-cutting it builds on, is declared done, and s99's write paths take the fleet-state derivation rather than the review pass."
  },
